  "notes": [
    "Fetch routes: fred.stlouisfed.org/graph/fredgraph.csv was blocked by the session allowlist; fred.stlouisfed.org/data/<SERIES> (the 'View All' table) worked for CSUSHPISA and HOSMEDUSM052N. FRED's SP500 CSV was blocked; S&P closes came from StatMuse, cross-checked against Dow Jones Data Talk (itiger) and Trading Economics. LBMA historical prices are no longer on gold.org (removed at IBA's request), so gold month-ends come from WGC's monthly commentaries.",
    "Gold basis: 9 of 13 points are WGC-published month-ends (5 explicitly 'LBMA Gold Price PM'; 4 cite Bloomberg/WGC without naming LBMA PM). 2026-06 and 2026-10 are spot closes from other sources. The total (-3.39%) compares an LBMA PM start to a spot end; a spot-to-spot comparison (StatMuse) gives -3.01%.",
    "Gold Oct 2026 uses Fri Oct 30 (Oct 31 is a Saturday). Trading Economics reports gold at its lowest since Oct 2025 that day.",
    "Housing series are monthly measures, not month-end prints. Case-Shiller runs to 2026-08 (Sep and Oct missing); NAR runs to 2026-09 (Oct missing). Their totals cover shorter periods than gold and the S&P.",
    "Benchmarks are price-only: S&P excludes dividends (total return would be higher); gold excludes storage and dealer spread; housing excludes rent, costs and leverage. Card portfolio comparisons should state whether card values are net of fees and grading costs.",
    "No figure here is estimated; every value is a cited published number. idx/pct fields are arithmetic on those numbers."
